{"case_id":"C030","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["fuzz-worthy entry point","input semantics","allocator-callback protocol","integer-boundary state"],"confidence":98,"affected_functions":["wuffs_base__malloc_slice_u8","wuffs_base__malloc_slice_u16","wuffs_base__malloc_slice_u32","wuffs_base__malloc_slice_u64"],"reason":"S1 adds four public memory-allocation helpers that accept attacker-variable-like uint64_t element counts, multiply them by element sizes, invoke a caller-supplied malloc-like callback, and construct typed slices. H0 only drives wuffs_gif__decoder__decode_image_config and wuffs_gif__decoder__decode_frame and performs its own direct malloc calls, so it does not exercise these new standalone APIs or their overflow, callback, and returned-slice invariants.","evidence":["The source explicitly says the wuffs_base__malloc_slice_uxx functions \"aren't used by Wuffs per se\", so GIF decoding does not inherently cover them.","H0 calls malloc(workbuf_len) and malloc(pixbuf_len) directly and never calls any wuffs_base__malloc_slice_u8, wuffs_base__malloc_slice_u16, wuffs_base__malloc_slice_u32, or wuffs_base__malloc_slice_u64 function.","Each helper has distinct boundary logic using num_uxx <= (SIZE_MAX / sizeof(uintxx_t)) followed by num_uxx * sizeof(uintxx_t).","Each helper accepts a nullable malloc_func and returns an empty wuffs_base__slice_uxx when the callback is NULL, the size is unrepresentable, or allocation fails.","Successful paths set .ptr to the callback result and .len to the original element count, whose semantics differ from the callback's byte-count argument."],"recommended_action":"Add a base-allocation fuzz target that selects among all four wuffs_base__malloc_slice_uxx APIs and fuzzes uint64_t element counts around 0, SIZE_MAX/sizeof(uintxx_t), and the first overflowing value. Use controlled callbacks covering NULL, allocation failure, and success while recording the requested byte count; assert that overflow cases never invoke the callback, failures return {NULL, 0}, and successes request exactly num_uxx * sizeof(uintxx_t) and return a slice whose len equals num_uxx."}
